    "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS/job/UAFS--University-of-Arkansas-Fort-Smith/Capital-Access-Business-Consultant_R0090014": {
      "title": "Capital Access Business Consultant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-20\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for “Find Jobs for Students”. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page.   Closing Date: Type of Position: Extension Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the   Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: ASBTDC - Provisional Positions Department's Website: https://asbtdc.org/ Summary of Job Duties: The Capital Access Business Consultant provides one-on-one consulting services to entrepreneurs and small business owners seeking business financing and capital resources. The position assists clients in evaluating financing options, improving capital readiness, preparing for financing applications, and navigating the process of obtaining business capital. This position serves both entrepreneurs seeking financing to start a business and existing small business owners seeking capital to stabilize or grow their businesses. The primary focus of this position is assisting clients with small business financing needs and supporting the State Small Business Credit Initiative Technical Assistance (SSBCI TA) program by increasing business financing applications and capital access outcomes. The consultant works with clients to identify financing needs, strengthen loan readiness, and connect businesses with appropriate capital resources. This UA Little Rock position is based in the ASBTDC regional office at the University of Arkansas - Fort Smith, with the employee's official work station at the UAFS Center for Economic Development in Fort Smith. The position may require work at the UAFS ASBTDC satellite office in Van Buren as needed and may also support small businesses in other areas of the state as organizational needs arise. This is a grant-funded position employed by the University of Arkansas at Little Rock in collaboration with the University of Arkansas - Fort Smith and is governed by state and federal laws and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Minimum Requirements Bachelor's degree in business, finance, accounting, economics, management, or a related field. Preferred Education/Experience Experience in commercial lending, banking, small business finance, accounting, business consulting, or entrepreneurship; Experience analyzing business financial information; Experience working directly with business owners or entrepreneurs; Knowledge of business financing programs and capital resources. Job Duties and Responsibilities Consulting Services Provide one-on-one consulting to entrepreneurs and small business owners seeking business financing and capital resources; Assess client financing needs and identify appropriate funding options, including commercial loans, SBA loans, microloans, CDFI financing, equipment financing, lines of credit, and owner investment; Assist entrepreneurs in understanding business formation requirements, licensing, permitting, and other startup activities that support capital readiness; Assist clients in the development and review of business plans, financial projections, cash flow forecasts, and financing documentation; Guide clients through the financing application process and assist them in preparing information requested by lenders and other funding partners; Help clients understand financing requirements, lending expectations, and available capital resources; Provide guidance regarding bookkeeping, financial recordkeeping, and other business practices that improve a client's ability to obtain financing; Assist clients in identifying and addressing issues that may impede financing readiness and recommend practical steps to improve their ability to access capital; Maintain current knowledge of financing programs, lending resources, and capital opportunities available to Arkansas small businesses; Identify consulting projects requiring advanced financial analysis or complex financing structures and coordinate with consulting staff possessing specialized expertise; Maintain accurate, complete, and timely client records that document client needs, consulting services provided, recommendations, progress toward business goals, and other required information in accordance with ASBTDC policies and documentation procedures.  Program Activities Assist with client recruitment, intake, and ongoing communication with prospective and existing clients; Provide professional, responsive customer service to prospective and existing clients by telephone, email, videoconference, and in person; Develop productive working relationships with lenders, resource partners, economic development organizations, and other organizations supporting small business financing; Participate in or deliver workshops, training programs, presentations, and outreach activities; Collaborate with the Fort Smith Regional Office and ASBTDC staff statewide to ensure clients are connected with the most appropriate consulting resources; Maintain timely and accurate documentation of client activities, work effort, program outcomes, and other required records in accordance with ASBTDC policies, documentation procedures, and funding requirements; Assist in implementing the ASBTDC marketing plan by identifying client success stories and supporting outreach activities; Assist with special projects and initiatives supporting the mission of the ASBTDC and the objectives of the SSBCI TA program; Participate in 32 hours of approved professional development annually; Perform other duties as assigned to accomplish the goals and mission of the organization. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of small business financing principles and capital resources; Knowledge of business planning, financial projections, and business startup requirements; Ability to analyze business financial information and identify financing readiness issues; Ability to explain financial concepts and lending requirements to entrepreneurs and small business owners in a clear, practical manner; Excellent verbal, written, and interpersonal communication skills; Ability to establish productive working relationships with clients, lenders, and resource partners; Maintain client records and program information in ASBTDC systems and ensure the secure and confidential handling of client information; Ability to manage multiple client projects while meeting deadlines and documentation requirements; Strong organizational skills and attention to detail; Ability to exercise sound judgment and maintain confidentiality; Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite and other business software applications; Ability to travel as needed to serve clients within the assigned service area and other areas of Arkansas as organizational needs require; Must maintain a valid driver's license and meet state requirements for operating vehicles on state business; Must adhere to the University System and ASBTDC Conflict of Interest standards. Additional Information: Salary Information: 63,000 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Heather Robinette, Entrepreneurial Services Manager, hbrobinette@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site  https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS   Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry, Substance Abuse Testing The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University’s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Driving, Standing, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Lifting, Pulling, Pushing Benefits Eligible: Yes"
    },
    "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS/job/UAFS--University-of-Arkansas-Fort-Smith/Adjunct-Faculty-Graphic-Design_R0080852": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty-Graphic Design",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-30\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for “Find Jobs for Students”. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page.   Closing Date: Type of Position: Adjunct Faculty Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Less than Annual Appointment (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Fort Smith University of Arkansas – Fort Smith The University of Arkansas - Fort Smith is a dynamic, mid-sized public university that’s redefining higher education. We’re on a mission to provide transformative, hands-on learning experiences for students of all backgrounds and aspirations. Our multi-faceted approach to education offers a wealth of opportunities, with over 70 academic programs, including certificates, associate, bachelor’s, and master’s degrees. We’re committed to building a diverse community that mirrors Arkansas’s rich tapestry, reflecting our dedication to serving the state’s varied population while enhancing the quality of our institution. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life, and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10 percent of employee salary.   Fort Smith, Arkansas Nestled along the Arkansas River, this vibrant city offers a perfect blend of history, culture, and natural beauty. Immerse yourself in the rich heritage of the Old West at the Fort Smith National Historic Site, explore the eclectic local art scene, or take a scenic stroll along the picturesque riverfront trails. With a welcoming community, diverse dining options, and a thriving downtown, Fort Smith is the ideal destination for history enthusiasts and those seeking modern amenities. Thank you for your interest in joining our university. Below you will find details for the position including any supplementary documentation and/or questions you should review before submitting your application. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (479) 788-7080. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 479-788-7080. Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. Department: Art and Graphic Design Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Teach in one of the following subject areas as assigned: Graphic Design This is a pool position. Applicants will be contacted as positions become available. The position reports to the department head/program director/dean who assigns responsibilities regarding student needs and course outcomes. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Work Experience: Qualifications of instructors teaching in the classroom for both lower and/or upper-level courses leading to an associate or bachelor’s degree requires a master’s degree in the discipline or related field with a minimum of 18 graduate credits in the subject area. Courses leading to a master’s require a doctorate degree. Adjunct faculty with a clinical assignment must be prepared at the level required by accreditation.  Instructors in occupational and technical areas are generally required to have a minimum of an associate’s degree and related work experience. Other job-related education and/or experience may be substituted for part of these requirements. Preferred Education and/or Work Experience: Prior teaching experience. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: To perform the job successfully, the following competencies are required for the essential functions of this position: Current knowledge of the relevant discipline.  Good organizational skills and timeliness in responding to student inquiries.  Ability to respond to needs of learners from a variety of educational backgrounds in a multicultural environment.  Ability to deliver course outcomes and content through a variety of teaching/learning styles.  Ability to use technology effectively in teaching.  Ability to communicate effectively both orally and in writing.  Ability to establish and maintain effective interpersonal relationships with students and colleagues.  This is a pool position. Applicants will be contacted as positions become available. Job Responsibilities Classroom and online instruction Assess and evaluate student learning Responsible for maintaining a positive work atmosphere by acting and communicating in a manner to foster teamwork and by providing leadership to subordinates. Requires consistent on-time attendance. Other duties as assigned. Additional Information: Salary Information: Dependent upon department. Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: HR 479-788-7080 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site  https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS   Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position may be subject to a pre-employment criminal background check, sex offender registry check, financial history background check, and/or drug screening. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication and/or adverse financial history alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background checks and drug screening information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University’s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: No"
    },
    "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS/job/UAFS--University-of-Arkansas-Fort-Smith/Resident-Director--Sebastian-Commons_R0089057": {
      "title": "Resident Director, Sebastian Commons",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-29\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for “Find Jobs for Students”. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page.   Closing Date: Type of Position: Professional Staff - Student Affairs Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Fort Smith University of Arkansas – Fort Smith The University of Arkansas - Fort Smith is a dynamic, mid-sized public university that’s redefining higher education. We’re on a mission to provide transformative, hands-on learning experiences for students of all backgrounds and aspirations. Our multi-faceted approach to education offers a wealth of opportunities, with over 70 academic programs, including certificates, associate, bachelor’s, and master’s degrees. We’re committed to building a diverse community that mirrors Arkansas’s rich tapestry, reflecting our dedication to serving the state’s varied population while enhancing the quality of our institution. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life, and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10 percent of employee salary.   Fort Smith, Arkansas Nestled along the Arkansas River, this vibrant city offers a perfect blend of history, culture, and natural beauty. Immerse yourself in the rich heritage of the Old West at the Fort Smith National Historic Site, explore the eclectic local art scene, or take a scenic stroll along the picturesque riverfront trails. With a welcoming community, diverse dining options, and a thriving downtown, Fort Smith is the ideal destination for history enthusiasts and those seeking modern amenities. Thank you for your interest in joining our university. Below you will find details for the position including any supplementary documentation and/or questions you should review before submitting your application. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (479) 788-7080. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 479-788-7080. Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. Department: Housing and Residential Life Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Sebastian Commons Resident Director is a full-time live-in position that reports directly to Assistant Dean of Students for Housing & Campus and Community Engagement. As a member of the Student Affairs staff, they are responsible for the general welfare of all students, encouraging them to maximize their intellectual growth and personal development. They are expected to positively influence, contribute to, and improve the quality of life of the residential student through the residential curriculum, implementing college policies and procedures, and by forming relationships with students in their facility. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Work Experience: Minimum requirements include a bachelor's degree with at least one year significant experience in a student housing employment position or equivalent experience. The position requires knowledge and skills related to human development, programming, conflict resolution, and the fair application of regulations. Other job-related education and/or experience may be substituted for part of these requirements. Preferred Education and/or Work Experience: Candidates with a master's degree in college student personnel, educational administration, or a related field, and previous experience supervising resident assistants, working with a residence hall association, and working with peer student conduct systems are preferred. Excellent verbal and written communication skills, the ability to work with diverse populations effectively, and excellent customer service skills are all expected. Essential Job Duties and Responsibilities: Supervise 8 Resident Assistants through weekly staff meetings, biweekly 1 on 1s, monitoring programming and community development, and semester evaluations Assist in hiring and training of Resident Assistants and other university staff as appointed Participate in the development, coordination and implementation of Housing & Residential Life procedures and programs Coordinate the assignments, contract, and billing processes for Sebastian Commons residents Serve as a University Conduct Administrator. Serve as a conduct officer for assigned residential area. Inform Assistant Dean of Students for Housing & Campus and Community Engagement of any issues. Serve in an on-call capacity with other HRL professional staff. Respond to all situations by answering phone, working with Resident Assistant On Call, and communicating with applicable staff such as the University Police Department, state and local emergency personnel, Assistant Dean of Students for Housing & Campus and Community Engagement and any chief student affairs officer positions. Supervise front desk/ office operations including supervising RAs and student workers in the office, receiving mail and packages, communicating with residents and visitors, and answering the phone Coordinate all move in and move out times and processes. Includes inspection of each room after the students have vacated and before it is occupied again, distribution and collection of applicable housing forms, and timely communication to residents Ensure that the quality and cleanliness of residential area, including outdoor property, is maintained Work jointly with Assistant Dean of Students for Housing & Campus and Community Engagement and Director of Facilities and Environmental Safety to ensure ongoing upkeep of facilities, custodial needs, maintenance efforts, and timely responses to work order requests Coordinate lock and key changes with maintenance and track all key use, loss, and theft Conduct quarterly Health & Safety Inspections of all rooms with the help of Resident Assistants. Document all work order needs and damage. Address any conduct violations. Implement, interpret, and continually develop HRL policies as stated in the Residential Handbook and Student Code of Conduct Serve as a Campus Security Authority (CSA) by understanding and following FERPA, Title IX, and the Clery Act as they pertain to on campus situations. Serve as a mandatory reporter and be trained in Title IX policy. Serve as first-level contact for parents regarding student housing needs and resident concerns Coordinate room changes and consolidation throughout the year Assist in development and implementation of campus emergency and crisis management procedures, programs, and services Assist residents with approved ADA accommodations based on need Maintain residential area budget Maintain confidentiality of all student information Review and create reports on an as-needed basis Establish Resident Assistant On Call schedule by ensuring staff availability for evenings, nights, and weekends Supervise and train summer part-time staff Advise the Resident Assistant Council Serve as the Housing and Residential Life website editor Supervise the HRL Social Media Student Assistant. Other Job Duties and Responsibilities: Adhere to the University of Arkansas – Fort Smith Employee Handbook Requires consistent on-time attendance Responsible for maintaining a positive work atmosphere by acting and communicating in a manner to foster teamwork and to provide leadership to subordinates. Identify student rooms to serve as tour rooms for Admissions and ensure those rooms are ready when needed Attend all University trainings, as required Take part in university and/or departmental committees as required by the department of Student Affairs or for professional development Advise a hall government system and/or Residence Hall Association Other duties as assigned. Responsible for maintaining a positive work atmosphere by acting and communicating in a manner to foster teamwork and by providing leadership to subordinates. Requires consistent on-time attendance. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: To perform the job successfully, the following competencies are required for the essential functions of this position: Conflict resolution Knowledge of university structures and governance Budget projections and management Communicate well with very diverse constituents Teaching and facilitating with individuals and groups Ability to apply conduct regulations fairly and consistently Ability to identify and draw on resources across campus Skills in conceiving, designing, and implementing educational programming Knowledge of laws and procedures related to university housing Ability to balance and respect individual rights and community rights Knowledge of learning processes and commitment to foster student learning Adaptability – adapts to changes in the work environment, manages competing demands and is able to deal with frequent change, delays or unexpected events. Dependability – is consistently at work and on time, follows instructions, responds to management direction and solicits feedback to improve performance. Knowledge of the principles of computer operations to understand the college’s information systems and services which carry out accounting, budgeting, purchasing, human resources, enrollment, and other or similar centralized institution-wide management information functions.    Additional Information: Working Relationships: Work in a dynamic team of diverse faculty, staff, and students in a fast paced, growth-oriented environment. Frequent contact with vendors, personnel from other agencies and institutions and the general public, student employees, resident assistants, professional staff in student affairs, housing and residential life professional staff, custodial and grounds workers, maintenance workers, faculty, parents, student residents.   List Employees Supervised: Resident Assistants (8), Social Media Student Assistant (1), Summer Housing Managers (3), Summer Facility Workers (2) Special Job Dimensions: Modest travel required for professional development and accompanying student groups; modest physical demands and stamina needed in working with resident assistants, programming materials, move-ins, on call, etc.; Required abilities include walking, standing, and sitting for extended periods. Visual demands include close, relatively detailed vision when focusing on a computer screen; hours are traditional office hours with evening meetings and programs and on call responsibilities in the overnight, weekends, and holidays; live-in is required. Background Check Requirements. Criminal Background Check, Financial Background Check, and Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) Check ; Position requires employee complete Arkansas Mandated Reporter training prior to employment. This job description is not designed to contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties, and/or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. Salary Information: $37,745.05 plus additional benefits: Furnished apartment to include utilities, wired and wireless internet, reserved parking space, unlimited meal plan, $1,000 in Lion's Cash Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Full consideration will be given to applications received by August 14, 2026. Recruitment Contact Information: HR 479-788-7080 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site  https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS   Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position may be subject to a pre-employment criminal background check, sex offender registry check, financial history background check, and/or drug screening. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication and/or adverse financial history alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background checks and drug screening information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University’s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"
    },
