    "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS/job/UAFS--University-of-Arkansas-Fort-Smith/Admissions-Processing-Specialist_R0092845": {
      "title": "Admissions Processing Specialist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for “Find Jobs for Students”. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page.   Closing Date: Type of Position: Staff - Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Fort Smith University of Arkansas – Fort Smith The University of Arkansas - Fort Smith is a dynamic, mid-sized public university that’s redefining higher education. We’re on a mission to provide transformative, hands-on learning experiences for students of all backgrounds and aspirations. Our multi-faceted approach to education offers a wealth of opportunities, with over 70 academic programs, including certificates, associate, bachelor’s, and master’s degrees. We’re committed to building a diverse community that mirrors Arkansas’s rich tapestry, reflecting our dedication to serving the state’s varied population while enhancing the quality of our institution. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life, and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10 percent of employee salary.   Fort Smith, Arkansas Nestled along the Arkansas River, this vibrant city offers a perfect blend of history, culture, and natural beauty. Immerse yourself in the rich heritage of the Old West at the Fort Smith National Historic Site, explore the eclectic local art scene, or take a scenic stroll along the picturesque riverfront trails. With a welcoming community, diverse dining options, and a thriving downtown, Fort Smith is the ideal destination for history enthusiasts and those seeking modern amenities. Thank you for your interest in joining our university. Below you will find details for the position including any supplementary documentation and/or questions you should review before submitting your application. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (479) 788-7080. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 479-788-7080. Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. Department: Admissions Operations Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Admissions Operations Specialist is responsible for supporting undergraduate admissions operations, application processing, and student data integrity. The position is responsible for processing admissions applications and related documents, supporting identity verification and direct admissions processes, and identifying application and data integrity issues. Qualifications: Qualifications Required Education and/or Work Experience: Minimum qualifications include a high school diploma or equivalent; plus one year of specialized training and/or experience in a related clerical field. Other job-related education and/or experience may be substituted for part of these requirements.   Preferred Education and/or Work Experience: Associate degree or higher in office administration or business administration and/or experience in a related field is preferred.     Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Admissions and Application Processing  Process Direct Admissions applications and support related admissions processing activities.  Process Arkansas ACCESS applications and ensure applications are reviewed and processed accurately and timely.  Process and review application documents, including transcripts, test scores, immunization records, requisitions, financial documents, and other required admissions documentation to ensure required information is complete, accurate, and consistent with university admissions requirements. Identify potentially fraudulent applicants and assist with the identity verification process. Monitor application processes and identify opportunities to improve the applicant's experience and operational efficiency and assist with troubleshooting issues to streamline the experience.  Assist with data integrity and record management, including a review of duplicate records. Evaluate existing application and admissions processes and recommend improvements that promote operational efficiency, data accuracy, and a positive applicant experience.  Maintain knowledge of university admissions policies, application requirements, CRM functionality, and related systems.  Perform other duties and special projects as assigned.  Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities  Knowledge of admissions and student application processes.  Ability to work with CRM and Student Information System environments.  Strong attention to detail and commitment to data accuracy.  Ability to analyze data and identify discrepancies, duplicates, and process errors.  Strong problem-solving and troubleshooting skills.  Ability to interpret application requirements, business processes, and system functionality.  Ability to manage multiple priorities and meet established deadlines.  Strong written and verbal communication skills.  Ability to communicate technical and system-related information to users with varying levels of technical experience.  Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with university departments and colleagues.  Ability to maintain confidentiality when working with student and institutional data.  Ability to learn new systems, applications, and processes quickly.  Preferred Qualifications  Experience working with a higher education CRM, particularly Slate or a similar admissions CRM.  Experience with student information systems such as Workday, Banner, PeopleSoft, or similar systems.  Experience processing college admissions applications and supporting enrollment processes.  Experience with data integrity, duplicate record management, and data auditing.  Experience writing or running database queries and reports.  Experience working with system integrations or data migration processes.  Experience with application configuration, testing, and process improvement.  Key Areas of Responsibility  Undergraduate Admissions Application and Document Processing  Duplicate Record Identification and Consolidation  Application Document Processing    Qualification Equivalencies: Additional Information: Salary Information: $31,315 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Full consideration will be given to applications received by October 31, 2026. Recruitment Contact Information: HR 479-788-7080 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site  https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS   Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check This position may be subject to a pre-employment criminal background check, sex offender registry check, financial history background check, and/or drug screening. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication and/or adverse financial history alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background checks and drug screening information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University’s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Hearing Occasional Physical Activity: Sitting Benefits Eligible: Yes"
    },
    "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS/job/UAFS--University-of-Arkansas-Fort-Smith/Public-Safety-Dispatcher_R0093111": {
      "title": "Public Safety Dispatcher",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for “Find Jobs for Students”. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page.   Closing Date: Type of Position: Staff - Public Safety Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Fort Smith University of Arkansas – Fort Smith The University of Arkansas - Fort Smith is a dynamic, mid-sized public university that’s redefining higher education. We’re on a mission to provide transformative, hands-on learning experiences for students of all backgrounds and aspirations. Our multi-faceted approach to education offers a wealth of opportunities, with over 70 academic programs, including certificates, associate, bachelor’s, and master’s degrees. We’re committed to building a diverse community that mirrors Arkansas’s rich tapestry, reflecting our dedication to serving the state’s varied population while enhancing the quality of our institution. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life, and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10 percent of employee salary.   Fort Smith, Arkansas Nestled along the Arkansas River, this vibrant city offers a perfect blend of history, culture, and natural beauty. Immerse yourself in the rich heritage of the Old West at the Fort Smith National Historic Site, explore the eclectic local art scene, or take a scenic stroll along the picturesque riverfront trails. With a welcoming community, diverse dining options, and a thriving downtown, Fort Smith is the ideal destination for history enthusiasts and those seeking modern amenities. Thank you for your interest in joining our university. Below you will find details for the position including any supplementary documentation and/or questions you should review before submitting your application. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (479) 788-7080. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 479-788-7080. Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. Department: University Police Department Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Public Safety Dispatcher works under general supervision in a team-oriented setting and is responsible for providing central dispatch services for the University Police Department (UPD). This position is governed by law enforcement standards and departmental and institutional policy. The position reports to the Chief of Police. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Work Experience: Minimum requirements include high school diploma or equivalent; plus one year of experience in the operation of public safety or related communication equipment; a stable work history; and a valid driver’s license.  Previous dispatch experience in a non-public safety related field may be considered. Must have or obtain ACIC/NCIC computer training and certification. Other job related education and/or experience may be substituted for part of these requirements.. Essential Job Duties and Responsibilities: Receives emergency and non-emergency calls for service, determines the nature and severity of calls received, and initiates the appropriate response, to include dispatching UPD officers and requesting response from fire department, emergency medical, or other agency police personnel. (60%) Uses computers/database to retrieve driver’s license and vehicle information, check for warrants, and access other law enforcement data, and issues parking permits. (20%) Monitors and records the status of patrol officers, maintains accurate log of calls for service and response activity, and assists officers with report entry. (14%) Completes various administrative tasks. (4%) Responsible for maintaining a positive work atmosphere by acting and communicating in a manner to foster teamwork and by providing leadership to subordinates. Requires consistent on-time attendance. Other Job Duties and Responsibilities (2%): Other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: To perform the job successfully, the following competencies are required for the essential functions of this position: Understands communications equipment and usage procedures. Understands emergency response procedures and is able to remain calm and perform effectively during stressful, emergency episodes. Effective interpersonal skills and communication techniques. Strong oral and written communication skills.  Ability to work under minimal supervision. Understands modern office equipment and procedures. Ability to deal with diverse populations in a positive manner. Ability to maintain and honor confidentiality as required by law. Qualification Equivalencies: Applicable equivalencies may be considered on the qualification listed above. Additional Information: Working Relationships: Has frequent contact with departmental personnel; various public safety officials; University staff, faculty, and students; and local residents; and works in a culturally diverse environment. List Employees Supervised: None. Special Job Dimensions: Work performed primarily in an office setting. While performing the duties of this job, the employee regularly exhibits digital dexterity when entering data into computer. The employee frequently sits for extended periods of time, and occasionally stands and walks. Vision demands include close, relatively detailed vision when focusing on a computer screen. Employee regularly talks and hears. Employee occasionally lifts items up to 10 pounds. Occasional shift work and schedule flexibility required. Dispatcher shifts are commonly 8:00 a.m. to 4:00 p.m.,4:00 p.m. to 12:00 a.m. and 12:00 a.m. to 8:00 a.m. Background Check Requirements. Criminal background check, financial history background check, sex offender registry check, MVR (Motor Vehicle Registry) check, drug screening, physical and psychological examinations. This job description is not designed to contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties, and/or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. Salary Information: $33,000-$36,000 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: HR 479-788-7080 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site  https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS   Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Financial Credit Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check This position may be subject to a pre-employment criminal background check, sex offender registry check, financial history background check, and/or drug screening. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication and/or adverse financial history alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background checks and drug screening information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University’s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Benefits Eligible: Yes"
    },
    "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS/job/UAFS--University-of-Arkansas-Fort-Smith/Assistant-Professor--Music-Education_R0093087": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Music Education",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-27\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for “Find Jobs for Students”. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page.   Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Non-Tenure Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Fort Smith University of Arkansas – Fort Smith The University of Arkansas - Fort Smith is a dynamic, mid-sized public university that’s redefining higher education. We’re on a mission to provide transformative, hands-on learning experiences for students of all backgrounds and aspirations. Our multi-faceted approach to education offers a wealth of opportunities, with over 70 academic programs, including certificates, associate, bachelor’s, and master’s degrees. We’re committed to building a diverse community that mirrors Arkansas’s rich tapestry, reflecting our dedication to serving the state’s varied population while enhancing the quality of our institution. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life, and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10 percent of employee salary.   Fort Smith, Arkansas Nestled along the Arkansas River, this vibrant city offers a perfect blend of history, culture, and natural beauty. Immerse yourself in the rich heritage of the Old West at the Fort Smith National Historic Site, explore the eclectic local art scene, or take a scenic stroll along the picturesque riverfront trails. With a welcoming community, diverse dining options, and a thriving downtown, Fort Smith is the ideal destination for history enthusiasts and those seeking modern amenities. Thank you for your interest in joining our university. Below you will find details for the position including any supplementary documentation and/or questions you should review before submitting your application. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (479) 788-7080. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 479-788-7080. Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. Department: Music and Theatre Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Department of Music and Theatre at the University of Arkansas – Fort Smith invites applications for the position of Assistant Professor of Music Education, Full Time Faculty beginning August 2027. The successful candidate will instruct undergraduate music education courses as well as other courses contingent upon the candidate’s expertise, interest, and department needs. The successful candidate will help promote student recruitment and be active in service to the university, community, and profession. The position reports to the Department Head of Music and Theatre. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Work Experience for Appointment as Assistant Professor: Terminal degree in Music Education or closely related field with valid active teacher license in Music. Demonstrated professional profile as an educator and scholar. Summary of Job Duties: Manage the music education program in the department. Work with the School of Education to facilitate communication between the faculty, students, and administration. Oversee student internships. Instruct music education courses, including, but not limited to, secondary instrumental methods and/or secondary vocal methods, introduction to music education, elementary music methods, and marching band and jazz techniques and/or choral literature. Teach other classes contingent upon the candidate’s expertise, interest, and needs of the department. Actively recruit to the department. Build positive relationships with area music educators. Participate in advising activities. Be active in scholarly and/or creative activities. Be active in service to the university, community, and profession. Responsible for maintaining a positive work atmosphere by acting and communicating in a manner to foster teamwork and by providing leadership to subordinates. Requires consistent on-time attendance. Other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: To perform the job successfully, the following competencies are required for the essential functions of this position: Expertise and experience in music education, including secondary instrumental and/or secondary vocal methods and elementary music instruction. Rules and regulations regarding teacher licensure Understand current research in music education Demonstrated excellence in collegiate teaching and recruitment Basic computing skills Ability to adapt to a changing environment Adept at using online platforms, including university systems and social media Have excellent interpersonal skills to work effectively with colleagues, students, staff, and the larger community. Active scholarly or creative productivity. Qualification Equivalencies: Additional Information: Working Relationships: In the typical workday, the successful candidate will interact with the faculty of the Department of Music and Theatre, faculty in the School of Education, students in the department, and occasionally faculty across campus. The successful candidate will also work with local music educators through student internships.   List Employees Supervised: N/A   Special Job Dimensions: Work performed primarily in an office and classroom setting. While performing the duties of this job, the employee regularly exhibits digital dexterity when entering data into computer, the skills necessary to be a music education expert, and has good interpersonal skills to work with students, faculty, and staff. The employee is active throughout the day requiring frequent standing. Vision demands may include close, relatively detailed vision when focusing on a computer screen. Employee regularly talks and hears. Employee occasionally lifts items up to 50 pounds. Routine work schedule Monday through Friday, often working nights and weekends.   Background Check Requirements. Criminal Background Check and Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) Check.   This job description is not designed to contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties, and/or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. Salary Information: $54,000 - $56,000 commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: HR 479-788-7080 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site  https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS   Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position may be subject to a pre-employment criminal background check, sex offender registry check, financial history background check, and/or drug screening. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication and/or adverse financial history alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background checks and drug screening information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University’s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"
    },
    "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS/job/UAFS--University-of-Arkansas-Fort-Smith/Assistant-Professor--Physics_R0093073": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Physics",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-27\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for “Find Jobs for Students”. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page.   Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Non-Tenure Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Fort Smith University of Arkansas – Fort Smith The University of Arkansas - Fort Smith is a dynamic, mid-sized public university that’s redefining higher education. We’re on a mission to provide transformative, hands-on learning experiences for students of all backgrounds and aspirations. Our multi-faceted approach to education offers a wealth of opportunities, with over 70 academic programs, including certificates, associate, bachelor’s, and master’s degrees. We’re committed to building a diverse community that mirrors Arkansas’s rich tapestry, reflecting our dedication to serving the state’s varied population while enhancing the quality of our institution. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life, and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10 percent of employee salary.   Fort Smith, Arkansas Nestled along the Arkansas River, this vibrant city offers a perfect blend of history, culture, and natural beauty. Immerse yourself in the rich heritage of the Old West at the Fort Smith National Historic Site, explore the eclectic local art scene, or take a scenic stroll along the picturesque riverfront trails. With a welcoming community, diverse dining options, and a thriving downtown, Fort Smith is the ideal destination for history enthusiasts and those seeking modern amenities. Thank you for your interest in joining our university. Below you will find details for the position including any supplementary documentation and/or questions you should review before submitting your application. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (479) 788-7080. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 479-788-7080. Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. Department: Physical Sciences Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The University of Arkansas at Fort Smith invites applications for a broadly trained physicist, atmospheric scientist, geophysicist, or astrophysicist. This Assistant Professor position will begin August 2027. The successful candidate is expected to: teach undergraduate level lecture and lab courses in calculus- and non-calculus based classical physics, physical sciences, offer courses in any area of physics related to their graduate expertise, mentor to undergraduate students, and develop a research agenda involving undergraduates. The Department of Physical Science is an interdisciplinary department that offers undergraduate degrees in Chemistry and Geoscience, and a minor in physics. The BS Geoscience program is a young program that is gaining national recognition through its culture of student involvement and undergraduate research. The chemistry program offers bachelor’s degrees following a traditional chemistry concentration and a biochemistry concentration. The physics program offers a minor in physics and plays a crucial support role for a number of majors both within the department and across the university, including advanced manufacturing engineering, electrical engineering, biology, and mathematics. Significant opportunities exist for developing new courses in physics, geoscience, atmospheric sciences, and even environmental studies. Primary responsibilities will be teaching calculus and non-calculus-based physics courses and associated labs. Additional teaching responsibilities may include physical science, other physics courses, and/or environmental or atmospheric courses related to the applicant’s area of interest and graduate experience. Other duties will include curriculum development supporting the physics minor, and/or the Geoscience and Chemistry degree programs, professional development, service to the department, college, and university including committee work, student recruitment and advising, and other related duties as required. The position reports to the Department Head of Physical Sciences. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Work Experience: Minimum qualifications include a PhD in any field of physics, atmospheric science, or geophysics with a minimum attainment of 18 graduate-level credit hours in physics. Candidates with demonstrated effective teaching experience in physics and/or closely related subjects and evidence of undergraduate research interests are preferred. Demands of the position require excellent oral and written communication skills; superior people skills; and the ability to utilize instructional technology in the classroom. Other job-related education and/or experience may be substituted for part of these requirements. Essential Job Duties and Responsibilities:   Strong undergraduate classroom instruction across modalities. Assessment and evaluation of instruction. Development and maintenance of a scholarly record which may include physics or science pedagogical methods Service to the department, college, and university, including committees and curriculum assessments. Responsible for maintaining a positive work atmosphere by acting and communicating in a manner to foster teamwork and by providing leadership to subordinates. Requires consistent on-time attendance.   Other Job Duties and Responsibilities:   Attendance and participation in all faculty and administrative meetings, Student Research Symposium, commencement ceremonies, and other meetings/events as required. Required employee professional development assignments. Other duties as assigned. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time, with or without notice.   Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities:   Ability to effectively teach a variety of undergraduate calculus- and non-calculus-based physics courses to non-majors. Ability to appropriately incorporate technology into classroom instruction to enhance student learning Ability to communicate effectively and professionally orally and in writing with students and co-workers Ability to interact with diverse groups of people in individual and team settings Ability to promote success in student learning with instructional methods that address a variety of learning styles Qualification Equivalencies: Additional Information: Working Relationships:   Must collaborate closely with coworkers in the Department of Physical Sciences to ensure the success of all departmental courses and programs. Will work daily with faculty, students, and staff in the College of Arts and Sciences and regularly with personnel across the campus. Interactions with students, teachers, staff, and administrators from Graduate Schools, K-12 schools and community groups will be required as needed for scheduled events.     List Employees Supervised:   Not applicable.     Special Job Dimensions: Work performed primarily in an office/classroom setting. Occasional travel and extended hours required. While performing the duties of this job, the employee regularly exhibits digital dexterity when entering data into computer. Required abilities include walking, standing, and sitting for extended periods. Visual demands include close, detailed vision when focusing on a computer screen. Employee regularly talks and hears. Employee occasionally lifts items up to twenty pounds.     Background Check Requirements. Criminal Background Check and Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) Check   This job description is not designed to contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties, and/or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time without notice. Salary Information: $54,000 - $57,000 commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: HR 479-788-7080 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site  https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS   Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position may be subject to a pre-employment criminal background check, sex offender registry check, financial history background check, and/or drug screening. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication and/or adverse financial history alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background checks and drug screening information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University’s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"
    },
    "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS/job/UAFS--University-of-Arkansas-Fort-Smith/Assistant-Professor--History-with-Teacher-Licensure_R0093080": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, History with Teacher Licensure",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-27\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for “Find Jobs for Students”. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page.   Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Non-Tenure Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Fort Smith University of Arkansas – Fort Smith The University of Arkansas - Fort Smith is a dynamic, mid-sized public university that’s redefining higher education. We’re on a mission to provide transformative, hands-on learning experiences for students of all backgrounds and aspirations. Our multi-faceted approach to education offers a wealth of opportunities, with over 70 academic programs, including certificates, associate, bachelor’s, and master’s degrees. We’re committed to building a diverse community that mirrors Arkansas’s rich tapestry, reflecting our dedication to serving the state’s varied population while enhancing the quality of our institution. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life, and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10 percent of employee salary.   Fort Smith, Arkansas Nestled along the Arkansas River, this vibrant city offers a perfect blend of history, culture, and natural beauty. Immerse yourself in the rich heritage of the Old West at the Fort Smith National Historic Site, explore the eclectic local art scene, or take a scenic stroll along the picturesque riverfront trails. With a welcoming community, diverse dining options, and a thriving downtown, Fort Smith is the ideal destination for history enthusiasts and those seeking modern amenities. Thank you for your interest in joining our university. Below you will find details for the position including any supplementary documentation and/or questions you should review before submitting your application. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (479) 788-7080. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 479-788-7080. Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. Department: History, Social Sciences, and Philosophy Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Department of History, Social Sciences, and Philosophy Department at the University of Arkansas – Fort Smith seeks applications for an Assistant Professor of History with Teacher Licensure. The Department offers four-year bachelor's degrees in both History and History with Teacher Licensure as well as minors spanning the breadth of the department disciplines. The department plays a significant role in supporting the general education curricula of the institution. The incumbent will teach 24 student credit hours during the 9-month contract year. The position will start August 9, 2027 and will report to the Head of the Department. Qualifications: Required Education and Work Experience: Ph.D. or ABD in History from an accredited institution of higher education and a current, active, secondary education teaching license in History, Social Studies, or related subject area. A master’s in history with a PhD in a closely related field would be considered. Ph.D. must be conferred by contract start.   Preferred Education and/or Work Experience: Prior College and High School teaching experience . Essential Job Duties and Responsibilities: Oversee the History with Teacher Licensure program, including: Instructing social studies secondary education courses, including teaching methods, practica, and in-school residencies Assess and evaluate student learning within the program Assist with program review processes and accreditation processes Build positive relationships with area educators Teach other history courses in person and online consistent with candidate disciplinary expertise and departmental need Develop and maintain an active scholarly research agenda based upon area of expertise that includes peer-reviewed publications Provide service to the department, college, and university as needed, including but not limited to assessment, curricula development, student recruitment, and shared governance bodies Maintain a positive work atmosphere by acting and communicating in a manner that fosters teamwork and collegiality.  Requires consistent on-time attendance. Other duties as assigned.   Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: To perform the job successfully, the following competencies are required for the essential functions of this position: Demonstrated knowledge of the relevant disciplines.  Good organizational skills and timeliness in responding to student inquiries.  Ability to respond to needs of learners from a variety of educational backgrounds in a multicultural environment.  Ability to deliver course outcomes and content through a variety of teaching/learning styles.  Ability to use technology effectively in teaching and service duties. Demonstrated excellent oral, written, and interpersonal communication skills. Ability to establish and maintain effective interpersonal relationships with students and colleagues. Qualification Equivalencies: Additional Information: This job description is not designed to contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties, and/or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. Salary Information: $54,000 - $56,000 commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Full consideration will be given to applications received by January 15, 2027. Recruitment Contact Information: HR 479-788-7080 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site  https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS   Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position may be subject to a pre-employment criminal background check, sex offender registry check, financial history background check, and/or drug screening. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication and/or adverse financial history alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background checks and drug screening information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University’s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"
    },
    "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS/job/UAFS--University-of-Arkansas-Fort-Smith/Assistant-Professor--Political-Science_R0093083": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Political Science",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-27\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for “Find Jobs for Students”. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page.   Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Non-Tenure Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Fort Smith University of Arkansas – Fort Smith The University of Arkansas - Fort Smith is a dynamic, mid-sized public university that’s redefining higher education. We’re on a mission to provide transformative, hands-on learning experiences for students of all backgrounds and aspirations. Our multi-faceted approach to education offers a wealth of opportunities, with over 70 academic programs, including certificates, associate, bachelor’s, and master’s degrees. We’re committed to building a diverse community that mirrors Arkansas’s rich tapestry, reflecting our dedication to serving the state’s varied population while enhancing the quality of our institution. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life, and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10 percent of employee salary.   Fort Smith, Arkansas Nestled along the Arkansas River, this vibrant city offers a perfect blend of history, culture, and natural beauty. Immerse yourself in the rich heritage of the Old West at the Fort Smith National Historic Site, explore the eclectic local art scene, or take a scenic stroll along the picturesque riverfront trails. With a welcoming community, diverse dining options, and a thriving downtown, Fort Smith is the ideal destination for history enthusiasts and those seeking modern amenities. Thank you for your interest in joining our university. Below you will find details for the position including any supplementary documentation and/or questions you should review before submitting your application. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (479) 788-7080. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 479-788-7080. Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. Department: History, Social Sciences, and Philosophy Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Department of History, Social Sciences, and Philosophy Department at the University of Arkansas – Fort Smith seeks applications for an Assistant Professor of Political Science. The Department offers four-year bachelor's degrees in both History and History with Teacher Licensure as well as minors spanning the breadth of the department disciplines. The department plays a significant role in supporting the general education curricula of the institution. The incumbent will teach 24 student credit hours during the 9-month contract year. The position will start August 9, 2026 and will report to the Head of the Department. Qualifications: Required Education and Work Experience: Ph.D. or ABD in Political Science from an accredited institution of higher education.  A master’s in political science with a PhD in a closely related field would be considered. Expertise in American governmental institutions and political science preferred. Ph.D. must be conferred by contract start. Essential Job Duties and Responsibilities: Teach other history courses in person and online consistent with candidate disciplinary expertise and departmental need, including general education American Government courses Develop and maintain an active scholarly research agenda based upon area of expertise that includes peer-reviewed publications Provide service to the department, college, and university as needed, including but not limited to assessment, curricula development, student recruitment, and shared governance bodies Maintain a positive work atmosphere by acting and communicating in a manner that fosters teamwork and collegiality.  Requires consistent on-time attendance. Other duties as assigned.   Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: To perform the job successfully, the following competencies are required for the essential functions of this position: Demonstrated knowledge of the relevant disciplines.  Good organizational skills and timeliness in responding to student inquiries.  Ability to respond to needs of learners from a variety of educational backgrounds in a multicultural environment.  Ability to deliver course outcomes and content through a variety of teaching/learning styles.  Ability to use technology effectively in teaching and service duties. Demonstrated excellent oral, written, and interpersonal communication skills. Ability to establish and maintain effective interpersonal relationships with students and colleagues. Qualification Equivalencies: Additional Information: This job description is not designed to contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties, and/or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. Salary Information: $52,000 - $55,000 commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Full consideration will be given to candidates who apply by January 15, 2027. Recruitment Contact Information: HR 479-788-7080 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site  https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS   Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position may be subject to a pre-employment criminal background check, sex offender registry check, financial history background check, and/or drug screening. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication and/or adverse financial history alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background checks and drug screening information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University’s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"
    },
    "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS/job/UAFS--University-of-Arkansas-Fort-Smith/Assistant-Professor--Criminal-Justice_R0093081": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Criminal Justice",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-27\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for “Find Jobs for Students”. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page.   Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Non-Tenure Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Fort Smith University of Arkansas – Fort Smith The University of Arkansas - Fort Smith is a dynamic, mid-sized public university that’s redefining higher education. We’re on a mission to provide transformative, hands-on learning experiences for students of all backgrounds and aspirations. Our multi-faceted approach to education offers a wealth of opportunities, with over 70 academic programs, including certificates, associate, bachelor’s, and master’s degrees. We’re committed to building a diverse community that mirrors Arkansas’s rich tapestry, reflecting our dedication to serving the state’s varied population while enhancing the quality of our institution. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life, and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10 percent of employee salary.   Fort Smith, Arkansas Nestled along the Arkansas River, this vibrant city offers a perfect blend of history, culture, and natural beauty. Immerse yourself in the rich heritage of the Old West at the Fort Smith National Historic Site, explore the eclectic local art scene, or take a scenic stroll along the picturesque riverfront trails. With a welcoming community, diverse dining options, and a thriving downtown, Fort Smith is the ideal destination for history enthusiasts and those seeking modern amenities. Thank you for your interest in joining our university. Below you will find details for the position including any supplementary documentation and/or questions you should review before submitting your application. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (479) 788-7080. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 479-788-7080. Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. Department: Criminal Justice Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Department of Criminal Justice at the University of Arkansas – Fort Smith seeks applications for an Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice. The Department offers a four-year bachelor’s degree and a minor in criminal justice. While the department offers online coursework, this is primarily an in-person position. Candidates are expected to teach face-to-face courses and maintain an active presence on campus. On-campus engagement includes but is not limited to holding regular office hours; providing academic advising and mentoring; participating in meetings; serving on committees and shared governance bodies; attending commencement and fulfilling other duties that require regular on-campus engagement and participation in the life of the university. The successful candidate will demonstrate excellence in teaching and service and an active research agenda that has the potential to result in published scholarly works or other peer-reviewed products. The position will start August 9, 2027, and will report to the Head of the Department. Qualifications: Required Education and Work Experience: Ph.D. in Criminal Justice or a terminal degree in a closely related field and a minimum of 18 hours graduate level coursework in criminal justice.  The degree must be from an accredited institution of higher education.  An advanced ABD will be considered but the degree must be conferred at the time of appointment.    Essential Job Duties and Responsibilities: Teach core courses within the Criminal Justice program, including but not limited to Introduction to the Criminal Justice System, Law Enforcement, Courts, Corrections, and Research Methods. Deliver instruction in multiple formats, including face-to-face, hybrid, and online modalities. Maintain an active scholarly agenda that includes peer-reviewed publications and other forms of academic scholarship. Provide service to the department, college, and university as needed, including participation in assessment activities, student recruitment and retention efforts, and shared governance. Advise and mentor students in support of their academic, professional, and career development. Maintain regular office hours. Foster a positive and collegial work environment by communicating and collaborating effectively with students, faculty, staff, and community partners. Demonstrate professionalism through reliable performance Perform other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: To perform the job successfully, the following competencies are required for the essential functions of this position: Good organizational skills and timeliness in responding to student inquiries.  Ability to respond to needs of learners from a variety of educational backgrounds in a multicultural environment, including first generation students. Ability to deliver course outcomes and content through a variety of teaching/learning styles.  Ability to use technology effectively in teaching and service duties. Demonstrated excellent oral, written, and interpersonal communication skills. Ability to establish and maintain effective interpersonal relationships with students and colleagues. Dedication to professional development. Qualification Equivalencies: Applicable equivalencies may be considered on the qualification listed above. Additional Information: This job description is not designed to contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties, and/or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. Salary Information: $52,000 - $54,000 commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: HR 479-788-7080 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site  https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS   Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position may be subject to a pre-employment criminal background check, sex offender registry check, financial history background check, and/or drug screening. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication and/or adverse financial history alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background checks and drug screening information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University’s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"
    }
  },
